{"success":true,"partial":false,"results":[{"id":"pull_request:openai/codex#719","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/719","title":"openai/codex#719","passages":[{"text":"This PR enriches the output of the `exec` subcommand, making use of color. It also introduces a new `--color=always|never|auto` option so the caller can control whether the output is colorized.\n\nI had to do a bit of experimentation with the `owo_colors` crate to figure out how to support this in a maintainable way because its `if_supports_color()` API is annoying to work with and `owo_colors::set_override(false)` doesn't do what you might expect. As you can see in `event_processor.rs`, I went with an approach where we define a number of `Style` objects that are \"empty\" when `with_ansi` is `false`.\n\nHere is the tail output of:\n\n```\n~/code/codex4/codex-rs/exec$ cargo run -- -m o3 'read the content of this crate and add an appropriate description to Cargo.toml'\n```\n\nimage\n\nthe\npr719\nbranch\n3 times, most recently\nfrom\n`8ef2b38` to\n`9579f05` Compare last yearApril 29, 2025 06:35\n\nmentioned this pull request\n\n[\\[codex-rs\\] fix: exit code 1 if no api key\\\\\n#697](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/697)\n\nthe\npr719\nbranch\nfrom\n`9579f05` to\n`65ec055` Compare last yearApril 29, 2025 06:54\n\nmarked this pull request as ready for review\n\nlast yearApril 29, 2025 06:54\n\nrequested review from\nfouad-openai and\noai-ragona last yearApril 29, 2025 06:54\n… (37 more lines)","truncated":true,"full_tokens_est":1054}],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"pull_request:openai/codex#2401","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/2401","title":"openai/codex#2401","passages":[{"text":"New style guide:\n\n# Headers, primary, and secondary text\n\n- **Headers:** Use `bold`. For markdown with various header levels, leave in the `#` signs.\n- **Primary text:** Default.\n- **Secondary text:** Use `dim`.\n\n# Foreground colors\n\n- **Default:** Most of the time, just use the default foreground color. `reset` can help get it back.\n- **Selection:** Use ANSI `blue`. (Ed & AE want to make this cyan too, but we'll do that in a followup since it's riskier in different themes.)\n- **User input tips and status indicators:** Use ANSI `cyan`.\n- **Success and additions:** Use ANSI `green`.\n- **Errors, failures and deletions:** Use ANSI `red`.\n- **Codex:** Use ANSI `magenta`.\n\n# Avoid\n\n- Avoid custom colors because there's no guarantee that they'll contrast well or look good on various terminal color themes.\n- Avoid ANSI `black`, `white`, `yellow` as foreground colors because the terminal theme will do a better job. (Use `reset` if you need to in order to get those.) The exception is if you need contrast rendering over a manually colored background.\n\n(There are some rules to try to catch this in `clippy.toml`.)\n\nae-openai\n\nadded 7 commits\n10 months agoAugust 17, 2025 17:46\n\n`\n          fix: remove non-ANSI colors\n`\n\n`\n          f273909\n`\n… (96 more lines)","truncated":true,"full_tokens_est":750}],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#12890","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/12890","title":"`ansi` theme is rendered as explicit RGB colors instead of terminal ANSI palette indices#12890","passages":[{"text":"# `ansi` theme is rendered as explicit RGB colors instead of terminal ANSI palette indices\\#12890\n\n#13016\n\n#13016\n\n## Description\n\ntummetott\n\n### What version of Codex CLI is running?\n\ncodex-cli 0.105.0\n\n### What subscription do you have?\n\nPro\n\n### Which model were you using?\n\ngpt-5.3-codex\n\n### What platform is your computer?\n\nDarwin 24.6.0 arm64 arm\n\n### What terminal emulator and version are you using (if applicable)?\n\nWezterm\n\n### What issue are you seeing?\n\nContinuation of #1618\n\nWhen `tui.theme = \"ansi\"` is selected, the displayed syntax colors do not follow the terminal’s configured ANSI palette. The current behavior appears to render syntax highlighting with explicit RGB values, which bypasses ANSI index mapping in the terminal.\n\nSo in other words: the `ansi` theme is just another bundled theme that hardcodes random colors instead of using the ANSI-indexed terminal-palette\n\nRelevant code paths suggest this behavior is intentional in current implementation:\n… (640 more lines)","truncated":true,"full_tokens_est":7633}],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#12912","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/12912","title":"Codex CLI themes are genuinely unusable#12912","passages":[{"text":"# Codex CLI themes are genuinely unusable\\#12912\n\n#13016\n\n#13016\n\n## Description\n\nimmapolar\n\n**Codex CLI version:**\n\n0.105.0\n\n**Description:**\n\nThe `background` key inside `.tmTheme` scope rules for `markup.inserted`, `markup.deleted`, and `markup.changed` is completely ignored. The diff view always renders with hardcoded bright red/green backgrounds regardless of what's defined in the custom theme file.\n\n**Impact:**\n\nUnusable for anyone with a custom terminal color scheme. The bright hardcoded backgrounds cause serious eye strain and make it impossible to read the highlighted code. My eyes are begging for mercy.\n\ngithub-actions bot\n\nPotential duplicates detected. Please review them and close your issue if it is a duplicate.\n\n- Color diff in Warp terminal is unreadable in the new version (Windows) #12904\n\n_Powered by Codex Action_\n\nyep thats hardcoded in `codex-rs/tui/src/diff_render.rs`. very bad\n\n- Color diff in Warp terminal is unreadable in the new version (Windows) #12904\n\n- `ansi` theme is rendered as explicit RGB colors instead of terminal ANSI palette indices #12890\n\n#12749 (comment)\n\n- feat(tui): add configurable diff backgrounds ignatremizov/codex#1\n… (330 more lines)","truncated":true,"full_tokens_est":4137}],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#48068","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/48068","title":"TUI status line becomes monochrome despite status_line_use_colors=true in 0.156.x#48068","passages":[],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#48451","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/48451","title":"TUI: Hook systemMessage renders ANSI SGR escapes as literal text instead of styles#48451","passages":[],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#38575","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/38575","title":"TUI: set DECSET 2031 so an in-place terminal theme change updates the composer colours#38575","passages":[],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#12904","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/12904","title":"Color diff in Warp terminal is unreadable in the new version (Windows)#12904","passages":[{"text":"# Color diff in Warp terminal is unreadable in the new version (Windows)\\#12904\n\n#13016\n\n#13016\n\n## Description\n\ntomasmarekk\n\n### What version of Codex CLI is running?\n\ncodex-cli 0.105.0\n\n### What subscription do you have?\n\nPRO\n\n### Which model were you using?\n\ngpt-5.3-codex-xhigh\n\n### What platform is your computer?\n\nMicrosoft Windows NT 10.0.26200.0 x64\n\n### What terminal emulator and version are you using (if applicable)?\n\nWarp\n\n### What issue are you seeing?\n\nAfter installing the new version of Codex CLI, the color diff in Warp has become unreadable. This is not a Warp theme issue, I tried all themes that are natively available in Warp terminal.\n\nThe colors for bash commands look fine, but the diff itself is unreadable. I’m probably not able to provide more information than this.\n\n### What steps can reproduce the bug?\n\nImage\n… (538 more lines)","truncated":true,"full_tokens_est":7051}],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"issue:openai/codex#45163","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/45163","title":"TUI: startup-only palette cache leaves input unreadable after system light/dark changes (0.154.0)#45163","passages":[{"text":"# TUI: startup-only palette cache leaves input unreadable after system light/dark changes (0.154.0)\\#45163\n\n## Description\n\nlightninglu10\n\n### What version of Codex CLI is running?\n\n`codex-cli 0.154.0`. The startup-only cache is also present in upstream `main` at `a592c38c16cdd7623dacc9168926ebccedfb67d3`.\n\n### What subscription do you have?\n\nNot relevant to this terminal-rendering issue.\n\n### Which model were you using?\n\nModel-independent; observed in long-running Codex CLI sessions.\n\n### What platform is your computer?\n\nmacOS, Darwin 25.6.0, arm64.\n\n### What terminal emulator and version are you using?\n\nCodePress Terminal, a Tauri/xterm.js host configured to follow the system light/dark appearance. The host updates its terminal palette and answers OSC 10/11 queries. Exact host release not recorded.\n\n### What issue are you seeing?\n\nAfter the terminal changes between light and dark appearance while Codex is already running, the composer and previously rendered user-message blocks retain their old background colors. The terminal's default foreground updates, producing nearly white text on a pale background (or the inverse mismatch). Long-lived sessions become unreadable after an automatic macOS appearance change.\n\nRefocusing and redrawing do not refresh the cached palette. Restarting/resuming refreshes the startup colors, but the next appearance change can break the session again.\n\nThis follows up my earlier report **#37298**, which described a failed refresh permanently poisoning the color cache in 0.146.0. The current implementation has a different failure mode: focus-driven refresh has been removed entirely, so no transient failure is required.\n\n### What steps can reproduce the bug?\n\n1. Configure a terminal to follow macOS system appearance and start Codex while the terminal is light.\n2. Send a message so both a user-message block and the composer are visible.\n3. Change macOS appearance to dark without restarting Codex, or leave the process running across the automatic appearance change.\n… (104 more lines)","truncated":true,"full_tokens_est":3099}],"license":"Apache-2.0"},{"id":"pull_request:openai/codex#46069","url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/46069","title":"Use syntax theme colors for inline code and file paths","passages":[],"license":"Apache-2.0"}],"repos":[{"repo":"openai/codex","indexed":true,"types":{"issue":true,"pullRequest":true,"readme":true}}]}